WEBVTT

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.530
Marchioness Zenovia,

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:37.740
"Prime Minister Sirgis,
Kingdom of Soljest"
I hope you can forgive my arrival
unannounced and without invitation.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.660
Think nothing of it, Sir Sirgis.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.950
To what do I owe this pleasure?

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.580
It's about the letter
I sent the other day.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:50.880
We're concerned the trade goods Marden
is exporting to Delunio may be fraudulent.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.010
Fraudulent?

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:57.140
Oh, dear, I know not what you speak of.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.600
So you have no intention
of discussing the matter?

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.220
You leave me no choice.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.600
It seems I must speak directly
with the royal house of Natra.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.400
Is not the Natran crown prince
now visiting your land?

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.860
I see.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:19.120
If his meeting with me didn't go well,
he planned to speak with Prince Wein.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.410
In short, he has no respect for me.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:25.870
I'd like to murder him in the worst way.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.580
You wished to speak with me?

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.380
I am happy to oblige.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.220
I am Wein Salema Arbalest,
Crown Prince of Natra.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.890
Now, let's get down to business.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.220
This is about the goods being
exported to your kingdom?

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.930
Yes, indeed.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:51.440
I wish to halt the imperial-made goods
flowing into the west via Natra.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.650
The empire is the mortal enemy
of the Levetian religion,

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:57.030
and their trade goods are their vanguard.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:01.870
I realize that historically,
your kingdom has deep ties with the east.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.120
However, you are of Caleus's bloodline.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:08.040
As such, I ask that you act as
a respected member of the west.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.210
Yes, I do see your point.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:15.800
However, the goods we are
exporting are made in Natra.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.050
Such subterfuge no longer holds water!

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.430
For example,

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:24.140
that outlandish yellow attire
the youth of our land now favor.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:30.810
We've determined it is an imperial product
being passed off as Natran made.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.610
A truly devious deception.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.650
I am afraid I know not of what you speak.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:41.360
The Teachings of Levetia view the east
as full of barbarian hordes, does it not?

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.910
Do you think such barbarians
could produce goods

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.620
that please the refined
western tastes of Delunians?

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.500
Do you truly believe that?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.040
Th-That is...

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.260
This problem encompasses
more than mere trade goods.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:02.220
The empire is peddling goods to pilgrims
passing through the Mardenian region.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.810
As a descendent of Caleus,
surely you know this is wrong.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.850
Refraining from undue interference with
pilgrims is customary among Levetians.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:16.360
To ignore that is the same as
dragging our faith through the mud!

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:21.740
Well, it is your right to claim our policy
is a problem for the Levetian religion.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:26.580
But you are no more than a
follower of the faith, not a Holy Elite.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:33.210
As such, you overstep your bounds
by presuming to speak for the Levetians.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.880
Was there anything else
you'd like to say, Sir Sirigis?

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:43.680
I will return home to discuss the matter.
Let us revisit this at a later date.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:49.220
I will add one last thing.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.810
You <i>will </i>rue this day before long.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:57.570
Let us pray to God that day never comes.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:03.070
I am sorry you had
to endure that last night.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:06.120
I had not foreseen your attendance.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.790
Think nothing of it. It was worthwhile
if only to learn more about Sir Sirgis.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.870
But I don't think we've
seen the last of him.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.630
He'll no doubt ramp up
the pressure however he can.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.840
Never let your guard down.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.260
You can count on me.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:29.970
So this is Phithcha,
the Kingdom of Soljest's royal capital.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.230
I'd say they're doing quite well!

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.520
Like Natra, they are a northern kingdom.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.150
But their port is never icebound.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.940
Right. They can conduct trade year-round.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:44.110
And they have many foreign markets
open to their shipping.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:44.950
So then...

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.780
Marden will profit from
additional trade routes

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:51.410
if they can piggyback
on Soljest's maritime trade.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.370
How good of you to visit, young prince.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:59.340
I would like to sincerely thank you

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.090
for the invitation to your kingdom's
ceremony, Your Majesty.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:06.970
Don't be silly. Did we not work
together to liberate Mealtars?

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:12.220
And I have long wished to exchange
words with you man to man.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.440
Let us take this to the great hall.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:20.650
I always hold talks with
heads of state over a meal.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:29.570
It's a chore walking
with a physique such as mine.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:33.290
I usually move about on
the palanquin you see here.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:38.460
Being of the nobility means
doing what others cannot do.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:42.880
Only peasants think their
legs are meant for walking.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:48.340
If one is going to call oneself wealthy,
this is <i>the </i>way to move about.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.180
So you say, but--

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:51.510
Indeed.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:55.980
But one noble's calling is
not necessarily the same as another's.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.400
If you don't identify with mine,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:03.360
perhaps your calling lies elsewhere.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.400
My calling?

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.570
I can't imagine what that might be.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:14.620
In youth, we are drawn to many things,
and we succeed as often as we fail.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.750
But in time, we discover something.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:21.330
We discover the beast growing within

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.840
and what it is that beast wants.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:29.470
He'll likely propose that
we forge loose yet friendly ties.

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:29.880
"Soljest"            "Natra"
"Delunio"

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:29.880
He'll likely propose that
we forge loose yet friendly ties.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:34.350
"Soljest"            "Natra"
"Delunio"

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:34.350
That way, he can prevent Natra
from expanding further west

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:40.690
"Soljest"            "Natra"
"Delunio"

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:40.690
while possibly working with Delunio
with whom we have poor relations.

00:06:40.690 --> 00:06:45.650
My planned price for this was
a slice of their foreign trade pie.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:49.450
But as it turns out,
I may be able to parlay this

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:55.120
into a Natran-Soljester alliance
that can defeat Delunio.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.500
Natra can now mobilize
a considerable army.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.420
And with Gruyere at the fore,

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.590
we can rebuff the Levetians
if they try to interfere.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:06.380
Then we conquer Delunio
and divide its land between us.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.630
And if we increase
our trade cooperation...

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:12.390
Whoa! Maybe I really am a genius!

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:15.430
That settles it!
I should join forces with Gruyere!

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.930
This is no time to be thinking about food!

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.930
I've gotta focus!

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:25.480
And who might that be?

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:28.570
A pleasure to make your
acquaintance, Prince Wein.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:29.110
I'm King Gruyere's daughter, Tolcheila.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:32.610
"Princess Tolcheila, Kingdom of Soljest"
I'm King Gruyere's daughter, Tolcheila.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:39.620
I told you to remain in seclusion
while I entertained my special guest.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:43.830
But Prince Wein,
the talk of the continent, is here!

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:49.300
It would shame me as a proper lady
if I were unable to trade words with him.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:53.130
So I would ask that you
allow me to join in.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:56.890
From what I can see,
Gruyere and Tolcheila get along well.

00:07:56.890 --> 00:08:00.140
It would be to
my advantage to draw her in.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.020
Nothing would please me more.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:06.940
Very well, I shall explain each of
the many dishes we will be serving.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:09.940
You won't regret this, Prince Wein!

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.780
I will if those explanations are too long.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:15.870
After all, my path to glory
will only be paved

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:19.740
if I can get Gruyere
to agree to an alliance.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:25.750
We'll start with a
white fish and herb salad.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:28.130
The fish is caught in our coastal waters.

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:31.380
But it's delicate and
a challenge to keep fresh.

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:34.630
But its flavor can't be
beaten when it's fresh!

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:37.010
Please, enjoy!

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:39.560
This does look good.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.100
I mean, really good.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:46.150
But it does look rather pedestrian.
I was expecting fancier fare.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.110
It's kind of a letdown.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:52.030
No, it <i>is </i>a letdown.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:55.200
That is <i>good</i>!

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.950
Wait, hang on! How can it be <i>that </i>good?!

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:02.000
I mean, it's just a fillet from some
bug-eyed sea creature!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.330
So it's to your liking?

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.880
Yes, it is quite delicious.
I eagerly await the next--

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.090
Whoa, hold up!

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:12.090
I'm here to forge
an alliance with Soljest!

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:15.180
I shouldn't be obsessing
about the next dish.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.680
What the hell?! It looks so good!

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:21.220
This dish is served inside fruit
that has been hollowed out.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:25.350
It's filled with savory mousse and topped
with seafood, eggs, and other delicacies.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:29.230
It's a feast for the eyes and the mouth!
I give it 100 points times two!

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:31.820
No! I'm not here as a food critic!

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.900
I'm supposed to be...

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.460
The amazing pork flavor was enough.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.670
But they made it even better
by serving it on a sizzling griddle.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:56.680
They served two subtle dishes first
to ramp up the impact of the roast pig.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:02.060
Who knew they had such a
well-developed culinary tradition?!

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:03.810
But now that I do know,

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:08.020
I must learn all I can about
their food while I'm here!

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:12.020
Then I'll bring what I learned back to
Natra and see whether it will catch on!

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:15.610
If it does, this whole trip
will be totally worth it!

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.530
No, you imbecile!

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:21.740
You're supposed to be forging an
alliance with the Kingdom of Soljest!

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:23.200
Snap out of it, stupid!

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.500
It will be smooth sailing for Natra

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:29.250
if you're able to sway
Gruyere right here, right now!

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:34.550
I won't be defeated by mere food,
no matter how enticing!

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:38.800
I'm utterly defeated.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:42.050
You couldn't take your mind
off the food, could you?

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:44.810
My tummy hurts.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.640
But that was odd.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.020
Even if you did get
sidetracked by the food,

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:53.610
I'm surprised that Gruyere
didn't bring up any issues of note.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:57.070
I'll just have to speak
with him again tomorrow.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:59.360
The ceremony itself won't take much time.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:04.620
Yes. There's an opening ceremony,
then a closing ceremony two days later.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:10.870
A letter arrived from
Prime Minster Sirgis of Delunio.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:12.170
Another one?

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:16.130
He writes, "The Mardenian region
includes land that the Kingdom of Delunio

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:18.630
lent in perpetuity to
the Royal House of Marden."

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:21.720
"But now that the Kingdom
of Marden no longer exists,

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:23.890
the rights to that land are forfeit."

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:29.100
"They have therefore reverted to
our kingdom effective immediately."

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.480
We originally wished
to purchase that land.

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:37.480
But out of respect for Delunio,
we agreed to a loan in perpetuity.

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:41.320
This is absurd.
Tell them the answer is no.

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:45.530
But they may threaten us with an attack.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.540
We'll deploy our forces if need be.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:51.080
But we must avoid open war at all costs.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:55.340
I doubt they want that, either.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:00.880
And that hereby concludes
the opening ceremony!

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:06.930
King Gruyere, may I have a word?

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.430
Why, it's the prince.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:14.650
It's about time for breakfast.
Let us head to the great hall.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:19.150
Today's main course is a dish
beloved by our kingdom's people.

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:20.780
We call it an omelet!

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:24.910
We fry beaten eggs and
fold them around chopped vegetables.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:29.450
It's a delectable dish with the exquisite
flavor of eggs and flavorful veggies.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:32.370
That does sound delicious,
but before we eat--

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:35.170
Forgive me. I have a matter to attend to.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:37.250
Let us talk later.

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:39.500
Huh?

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.840
Wait. What?

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:45.010
What the hell?!

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:48.680
What's the matter, Prince Wein?

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:52.810
I was wondering if you knew
where King Gruyere might be.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:55.560
Well, his body may be
heavier than a boulder,

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:59.150
but his mind is lighter than a feather.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:01.740
Who knows what he's up to right now?

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.110
Huh?

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.200
Pardon me.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:16.460
P-Pardon me.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:19.460
Pardon me.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.170
P-Pardon me...

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.430
It doesn't add up.

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:29.300
Soljest and Delunio
have never been on good terms.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:35.310
So if Natra were to ally with Delunio,
it would upend the status quo.

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:38.150
That's why I thought Gruyere
invited us to the ceremony.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:42.280
He wanted to take the initiative
by forging an alliance with us.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:46.450
The king is clearly avoiding you.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:51.870
So the question is, why invite you
here if he doesn't seek an alliance?

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:54.370
The most likely objective is...

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:56.210
Assassination.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:14:00.960
Soljest must feel threatened
by the new, more dynamic Natra.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:04.090
So he seeks to throw water
on Natra's ambitions

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:06.720
by assassinating its de facto leader?

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:08.550
Could that be it?

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:13.310
Could be, but he's had plenty
of chances to take me out so far.

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:16.480
Why drag it out so long?

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:19.810
Does he plan on doing something
in Natra while I'm away?

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:24.780
No, whatever it is,
I bet it's happening right now.

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:27.400
Ninym! Prepare to return home at once!

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:32.200
Tell everyone to be ready
to leave as soon as I give the signal.

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.240
Highness!

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:39.540
Forgive me for knocking at this hour,
but I bear a message from His Majesty.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:52.680
The young prince!

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.760
You must forgive me.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:59.190
I knew you wished to speak
with me this afternoon.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:02.440
But what do you say we have that chat now?

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:03.820
By all means.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:07.280
Gruyere must be up to something,
and it can't be good.

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:10.110
If so, there's one thing I must do.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:13.950
I must make him clearly state
whether he seeks an alliance.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:17.910
All will be well if he does,
but if he doesn't,

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:21.830
I'll take him hostage and flee the city.

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:30.880
There's an extra seat.
You there, the prince's attendant.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.390
You should sit as well,

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:35.100
Huh? Wh-Who, me?

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:39.140
I am honored by
your attention and concern, but--

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:43.770
You're the Flahm rumored to be
in the prince's favor, are you not?

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:47.690
It's fine. I don't fret
over such trivial matters.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:51.780
Then I shall join you.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:16:00.290
Do my words surprise you?

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:05.500
Forgive me if this seems rude,
but, yes, it is a surprise.

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:11.220
The Levetian scriptures clearly state
that Flahms are the Devil's minions.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:12.930
Your Majesty is a Holy Elite.

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:17.140
Is it not sacrilegious for you
to sit down with a Flahm?

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:21.390
Those scriptures are but scraps of paper!

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:26.310
Are one's deeds in accord with God's will?
Is one walking a righteous path?

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:31.320
We all must consider such questions
and come to our own conclusions.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.160
That is certain to be a difficult path.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.990
But there are no shortcuts when
it comes to our covenant with God.

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:43.670
Are you saying you have concluded
that Flahms should be treated equally?

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.540
Yes, precisely.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:50.260
I may be king, but I believe
all people are of equal worth.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:54.380
What does it matter if they
have white hair and red eyes?

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:01.520
Yes, but does God allow
such interpretations?

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:06.060
If He does not,
I will find out when the time comes.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:09.690
To rest in eternal peace at God's knee

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:12.530
or burn forever in the flames of hell.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:15.410
That only one of these can be
experienced in the afterlife

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:18.910
makes them priceless beyond measure.

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:24.960
And only our God can deliver
that final judgment when we die.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:29.670
Neither scriptures nor sermons have
the right to make such pronouncements.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:34.050
He is one tough fellow.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:37.760
I admire you as a wise king
and an enlightened individual.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:39.640
And I'm now certain of one thing.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:44.930
Yours is the kingdom with
which Natra should seek close ties.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:48.310
Unfortunately, I must return home at once.

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:49.770
But before I do,

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:53.440
I would like to forge close ties
between Natra and Soljest

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:57.410
so that we may survive the
turbulence of these troubled times.

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:58.700
What say you?

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.170
Very well.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.170
I accept your proposal.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.880
Why do you look so shocked?

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:16.170
It's just, I didn't expect you to agree.

00:18:16.170 --> 00:18:17.510
I won't say this again.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:22.140
An alliance between
Soljest and Natra is a fine idea.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:23.810
What?! Seriously?!

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:27.310
You mentioned you had
to return home at once?

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.230
Y-Yes, well...

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:31.900
Then I mustn't keep you any longer.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:36.280
I see no problem with leaving
the details to those that serve us.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:38.450
O-Of course.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:43.410
We're grateful for your hospitality
during our stay, Your Majesty.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:46.540
I bid you farewell, young prince.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:19:00.050
Now, I can hardly wait to see
how my little charade plays out.

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:02.970
Wouldn't you agree,

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:05.470
Sir Sirgis?

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:11.560
I don't get it.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:14.020
I thought the king was up to something.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:19.950
And Soljest didn't attack us
on the way home as we had feared.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:22.490
What is going on?

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:26.160
Forgive the interruption, Your Highness!
I come bearing urgent news!

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:32.170
The Kingdom of Delunio has attacked
the Mardenian region near the border.

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:36.250
And in accordance with
its alliance treaty with Delunio,

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:39.840
Soljest has commenced a
military campaign against Natra.

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:42.050
Wein, does this mean...

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:45.930
Soljest has just declared war on us.

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:48.350
The more one pursues
the pleasures of life,

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:50.440
the more one seeks the rarest kind.

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.770
I take pleasure in battle.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:59.030
And our meeting in Mealtars and
the recent audience have convinced me.

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:00.780
That prince is a rare beast.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:04.240
There may be only one of
his kind on the entire continent.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:11.040
Prince Wein, I will devour you
with all my might!

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:14.830
I saw this coming from the start!

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:17.460
That God damn pig!

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.130
What the actual hell?!
How's this an alliance?!

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.590
I bet he knew it would
turn violent if he said no.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:24.930
So he spewed those empty words!

00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:28.060
And it was a verbal agreement,
which is easily broken.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:30.520
He's in the clear, damn it!

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.850
And it's not only Gruyere.

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:34.900
Sirgis got me, too!

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.440
Our only choice is to
quickly gather our forces

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:39.190
and face Soljest in battle.

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:42.990
But they will be
difficult to fight head-on.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:46.070
That means we have one more thing to do.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:48.790
And to do that, we'll need you-know-who.

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.660
Please forgive me, Your Highness!

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:54.620
It's my fault it came to this!

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:58.750
I shouldn't have responded
to Delunio's provocation!

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:01.090
I've resigned myself to my fate.

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:03.880
I shall accept whatever
punishment you see fit.

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:08.810
But if you grant me a chance
to redeem myself, I will not fail you!

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:15.980
Wait, I thought she was utterly
devastated and had given up.

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:17.730
What will you do?

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:21.110
I will seek reconciliation with Delunio.

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:25.280
Soljest entered this war because it
perceived a threat to its ally.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:28.530
So if Delunio and Natra
could work out their differences,

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:32.250
Soljest would no longer have
a reason to attack your kingdom.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:35.540
My vassals have already
set off for Delunio.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:39.420
And I have arranged for them
to meet with Prime Minister Sirgis.

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:43.420
Of course, reconciliation
may prove difficult.

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:47.090
But I have an idea that
may help make it happen!

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:49.600
I beg you! Please give me this chance!

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:54.480
Truth be told, I am shocked.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:57.310
To think you'd do what
I was going to suggest.

00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:59.900
And I didn't even have to ask.

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:02.230
Now we can move faster than I thought.

00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:04.280
Let's set out for Delunio at once.

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:05.700
Ninym, make ready.

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:07.950
Yes, Your Highness.

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:12.290
And what of me?

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:16.790
There's no time to divvy up
the blame right now.

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:22.050
And personally, I don't believe
you're responsible for this incident.

00:22:22.050 --> 00:22:27.380
If you can convince my liegemen
of that before this is all over,

00:22:27.380 --> 00:22:30.140
your punishment will be much lighter.

00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:32.680
Can you do that, Zenovia?

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:34.600
Yes, I can!

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:36.640
Then let's go!

00:22:36.640 --> 00:22:39.520
We're going to turn
everything upside down!
